# Oracly Development Rules

Product: `docs/AI_AGENT_GUIDE.md` → `docs/MASTER_DIRECTIVE.md` → `docs/DEVELOPMENT_CHARTER.md` → `docs/vision.md` → EPICs → `docs/OOS.md` → `docs/PRINCIPLE-001.md` → `docs/GOLD_STANDARD.md`. Architecture: `docs/architecture.md`.

## Before Writing Code

1. **Analyze first** — read existing files in the feature; grep for similar widgets/services before adding anything.
2. **Explain planned changes** — list files to create, edit, or delete and why, before editing.
3. **Reuse over recreate** — use existing widgets (`GlassCard`, `TarotResultCard`, `TarotResultCards`, `TarotReadingSection`, section widgets, etc.) before creating new ones.
4. **Never duplicate widgets** — one canonical widget per UI pattern; extend or compose, do not copy-paste layouts.

## File Size

- **Maximum 150 lines per Dart file.**
- If a file exceeds 150 lines, split into sections/widgets/services in the same feature.
- **Exception:** static data catalogs only (`major_arcana.dart`, suit data files) — do not mix UI into data files.

## Composition

- Prefer **small composed widgets** over large `build()` methods or monolithic screens.
- Screens orchestrate; sections layout; widgets render.
- Extract when a screen grows beyond ~100 lines of UI code.

## Placeholders

- **Never leave empty placeholder files** (0-byte or export-only stubs).
- AI scaffolds in `lib/features/tarot/` must be **implemented or deleted** in the same task — do not add new empty files.

## Feature Boundaries

- New work goes under `lib/features/<name>/`.
- Shared code belongs in `lib/widgets/` or `lib/core/` only if used by **two or more features**.
- Do not modify unrelated features in the same task.

## Quality Gate

- Run **`flutter analyze`** before marking a task complete.
- **Zero analyzer issues** required — warnings included if they fail CI.
- Do not commit with broken tarot/chat/home navigation paths.

## Tarot-Specific

- Result UI must use **`TarotResultCard` / `TarotResultCards` / `TarotReadingSection`** — no inline result layouts.
- AI logic belongs in **`tarot_ai_service.dart`**, not in widgets.
- State machine: prefer **`TarotController` + `TarotState` + `TarotPhase`** when wiring flows.

## Definition of Done

Must satisfy **`docs/GOLD_STANDARD.md`** (all 10 gates) plus:

- [ ] `flutter analyze` passes
- [ ] No duplicate widgets or empty files introduced
- [ ] Files ≤ 150 lines (or split)
- [ ] Existing code analyzed and reused
- [ ] Only in-scope files changed
- [ ] Proud to ship today
